{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes","id":407159,"title":"Special snowflakes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-15T17:33:55-08:00","id":407159,"title":"Special snowflakes","content":"How well does this actually work when using it In your games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3965-andresmo23","name":"Andresmo23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T20:18:38-08:00","id":407322,"title":"","content":"depends on just how &quot;special&quot; the character is I would think. What kind of special snowflake do you have in mind? Can you be more specific with the question?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T21:49:43-08:00","id":407387,"title":"","content":"I had a drug addict raging that all she wanted was a kitsune in Seattle for no reason other then it's kawaii des. She's long gone","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T22:11:47-08:00","id":407390,"title":"","content":"&quot;Special Snowflake&quot; is one of those terms that really is hard to treat as having a definition to simple answer the basic question posed.<br /> <br /> The problem with such terms is that they're essentially, &quot;taking a good thing too far,&quot; problems. But what's too far? Well that's on your group's tastes.<br /> <br /> I've played with people that wouldn't bat an eye at Lyrics of War's example and wonder what the issue was. I've played with people that would have tossed that player on their ass in a second as well.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, special snowflakes don't work because by definition they're concepts that don't work for your group because they take &quot;interesting odd ball concept,&quot; too far into, &quot;ruins the fun of everyone else by being too special.&quot; The issue then becomes where that line is for your current group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T22:12:30-08:00","id":407391,"title":"","content":"Not even once.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though - the player characters are already the protagonists, why add an extra-special layer of on top of that? While everyone else is going about their mundane lives - picking up milk, balancing the checkbook - they're going on adventures, or have a nemesis. Even the majority of &quot;splat&quot; NPC's keep it routine - somebody's gotta fill up the car, or drop off the mail.<br /> <br /> On that note, though, a single kitsune in Seattle wouldn't be too remiss. People travel; no big deal. It's another thing depending on how &quot;kawaii desu&quot; she wanted to play it, however. &quot;Raging&quot; and &quot;drug addict&quot; hints that it would have been bad.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T22:53:39-08:00","id":407420,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=407322#post407322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">depends on just how &amp;quot;special&amp;quot; the character is I would think. What kind of special snowflake do you have in mind? Can you be more specific with the question?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well what i meant was a charecter that was unique but (hopefully) not naturally immpossible, a modern white howler, camerilla tremere outside the paramid, hermetic that sees technocrats as correct but wants to channel science through magick (not a good example but couldent think of anything for mage). That sort of thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3965-andresmo23","name":"Andresmo23","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T02:28:18-08:00","id":407531,"title":"","content":"Generally, I try and work with the players to make their character ideas a possibility, so long as it doesn't interfere with the game, or derail plots. Ive had a werewolf game, where 1 player really didn't like the idea of Garou and wanted to play a Bastet. It wasn't that hard to work in honestly, and so wasn't a big deal. I've also been a player in a Werewolf game where 1 of the players was a Mage. Also worked out fine, I guess. Less well this time since the Mage couldn't keep up with the Garou in a lot of fields which impeded the pack sometimes, which was less fun for the Werewolf players. That's the sort of thing I don;t think I would've allowed were it my game.<br /> <br /> Basically, as long as the player doesn't expect the game to revolve around them specifically, and is willing to work with the ST, it can be done. If either of those fall through, then the player shouldn't be playing that character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T17:54:28-08:00","id":408370,"title":"","content":"I don't like that because it takes the game away from the other player characters. if it is a player introduced concept, then it hijacks the game as NPCs constantly react to the special snowflake and shifts attention of the game/ST to the player concept instead of the chronicle idea that ST originally intended. If it is the ST's idea and he intends the game to be about that, it still hijacks the game from the other players as it makes everything dependent on that one PC. If that player can't make it to game, drops out of the game, if the PC dies, etc., then the chronicle is disrupted.<br /> <br /> In general, special snowflake characters reveals a creative bankruptcy in the player who doesn't know what to do, or how to make the game interesting with an &quot;ordinary&quot; concept. We're already playing vampires, werewolves, or wizards - you're telling me this isn't special enough for you? This is usually a sign that the player is very demanding and wants continual attention from the ST and/or other players.<br /> <br /> I agree with idpersona's comments - good rules to live by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T19:18:18-08:00","id":408483,"title":"","content":"While I'm generally on board with all that... I kind of balk at the &quot;creative bankruptcy&quot; level of it. A lot of players are coming from differing backgrounds and expectations on what &quot;ordinary&quot; concepts even are. And sometimes special snowflakes are actually really creative even if we'd all agree that they'd be too disruptive in the game we're running.<br /> <br /> I once told a player in a Mage game that I loved their concept... but it was way too Shadowrun in a game intended to be a street level Revised MtA game. It wasn't a lack of creativity, or an inability to make interesting stuff. It was just a concept that was too over the top for the intended game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T00:55:53-08:00","id":408681,"title":"","content":"I have a rule, &quot;You will be no more special than any other PC&quot; So if you ask to play a white Howler throwback you don't get to bitch when someone ask to play an Apis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T07:10:01-08:00","id":408932,"title":"","content":"That seems a bit excessive.<br /> <br /> I get that &quot;special snowflake&quot; for a lot of people is by definition bad, but it's the sort of thing that seems best solved trying to talk to people, not enforcing some rule that ends up pitting players against each other.<br /> <br /> The point is to make a group of characters that are interesting and fun together in the story the ST runs, not get them after each other because someone wants a 7 point Merit or something while the rest don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T14:11:14-08:00","id":409317,"title":"","content":"Yeah special can only go so far though, then you wind up with someone trying to recreate sangos weapons from inu yasha and commenting about how they wished they had a rank 5 gift so they can be a puppy with glowing eyes (in sorry fianna fans! I didn't allow it!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T21:40:59-08:00","id":411026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=408932#post408932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems a bit excessive.<br /> <br /> I get that &quot;special snowflake&quot; for a lot of people is by definition bad, but it's the sort of thing that seems best solved trying to talk to people, not enforcing some rule that ends up pitting players against each other.<br /> <br /> The point is to make a group of characters that are interesting and fun together in the story the ST runs, not get them after each other because someone wants a 7 point Merit or something while the rest don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its probably not the best example. But my point is One player doesn't get to monopolize the special. I will make plot for the players. I am more than willing to let them be special, but if a player wants to be a snowflake and then bitches about other snowflakes well that's a problem. If you want to play a vanilla you pick vanilla. I will run vanilla, But I won't let someone decide &quot;I want to b ethe only chocolate in this game&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T05:51:00-08:00","id":411342,"title":"","content":"It can depend. Special Snowflakes can break the game but in other case it can enhance it.<br /> <br /> In my case my &quot;snowflakes&quot; are just quirky: A Tremere bruiser who is thaumaturgically inept or a Shadow lord who is a Black Furie born male Garou.<br /> <br /> They are special, but it's more &quot;flavor&quot; special than gamebreaking special.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T09:29:37-08:00","id":411674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=411026#post411026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am more than willing to let them be special, but if a player wants to be a snowflake and then bitches about other snowflakes well that's a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is still problematic to me. Players bitching about other player concepts for non-constructive reasons is bad regardless of snowflakes.<br /> <br /> If I made something that gets labeled &quot;acceptable&quot; snowflake... why do I lose a say in someone else making something that might be equally &quot;special&quot; but far more disruptive (or even less special but more disruptive)? How do you even start to fairly say where the &quot;levels&quot; of specialness even are? Why is a Howler throwback the same as an Apis? If I make a Silver Fang with equal claim to the throne as Albrecht with some Fate tossed in, is that less/more/equal in being special to having the Perfect Metis? Who gets to bitch about who's concept? What's the use of even allowing for this situation to be a possibility?<br /> <br /> Again, this seems like something that should be dealt with by having a conversation with your players; not telling one player they don't have a right to voice opinions regardless of the usefulness of those opinions because of their character concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T11:21:22-08:00","id":411815,"title":"","content":"With a good player and an attentive Storyteller, it works just fine.<br /> <br /> My Hunter: the Reckoning game features several, including a Hunter who has been Imbued for over a decade (the Imbued only became &quot;a thing&quot; ONE year ago), an Inquisitor who follows the Sanbenito heresy (they think some monsters can be saved), and a Japanese dhampir (yep, the most cliched special snowflake you can get). And believe it or not, all the characters are cool, work well enough together, and their uniqueness serves as minor plot points without detracting from the attention given to other player-characters.<br /> <br /> Now, with a bad player or an inattentive/inexperienced/just-plain-dumb Storyteller? Yeah, those are the situations that leads to people automatically assuming a &quot;special snowflake&quot; is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> I've seen those, too, especially when it is the Storyteller's fault. Like the situations where one character is clearly the &quot;main character&quot; and everyone else is a sidekick. Or the one time where the ST allowed the PC to be something special, then became obviously vindictive about it, as though trying to punish the player for choosing something interesting and different.<br /> <br /> So remember: If you are a player, spare a thought for everyone else's fun, and be gracious if your character concept is turned down. If you are a Storyteller, give careful consideration to what the player is asking for, and see if you can suggest a way to make it work in your story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":966,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","user":"Redford_Blade","date":". 02-19-2015, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T18:57:56-08:00","id":412310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=411342#post411342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It can depend. Special Snowflakes can break the game but in other case it can enhance it.<br /> <br /> In my case my &quot;snowflakes&quot; are just quirky: A Tremere bruiser who is thaumaturgically inept or a Shadow lord who is a Black Furie born male Garou.<br /> <br /> They are special, but it's more &quot;flavor&quot; special than gamebreaking special.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, those are just &quot;quirky&quot; and &quot;flavorful,&quot; like you said. Special snowflakes are the ones that don't fit organically into the setting, and don't have a desire to - they expect the setting to warp around them. They're the Gurahl Abomination that doesn't suffer from Harano in a Mage game. And that's fine if that's what someone and their troupe are into, but when one is informed about the setting and says, &quot;Nah, throw that away. Here's my thing,&quot; is when the problems occur.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","user":"nothing","date":". 02-19-2015, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T20:09:43-08:00","id":412370,"title":"","content":"My main character started off as a (DA:Fae) Changeling under the control of a cruel Tremere regent as a sort of &quot;pet&quot;, who was eventually embraced by the Regents childer as they both worked together to overthrow him (he wasn't too thrilled about the embrace part and that childer died not too long after). I would certainly consider him a &quot;special snowflake&quot; but as long as your coterie isn't a traveling freakshow of weird splats it's good to have each player have something somewhat unique to them and not just Brujah #7","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T01:38:51-08:00","id":412561,"title":"","content":"Most of al i find it depends on whether or not its actually a proper concept with nuance and feeling for how it works in the setting and what consequences it brings - or if its just somebody mashing shit up for coolness or to be special. The first can be a rewarding experience for all. The other is what makes Snowflakes something that should be closely monitors by the ST and possibly nipped in the bud.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T01:25:45-08:00","id":413909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=411674#post411674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is still problematic to me. Players bitching about other player concepts for non-constructive reasons is bad regardless of snowflakes.<br /> <br /> If I made something that gets labeled &quot;acceptable&quot; snowflake... why do I lose a say in someone else making something that might be equally &quot;special&quot; but far more disruptive (or even less special but more disruptive)? How do you even start to fairly say where the &quot;levels&quot; of specialness even are? Why is a Howler throwback the same as an Apis? If I make a Silver Fang with equal claim to the throne as Albrecht with some Fate tossed in, is that less/more/equal in being special to having the Perfect Metis? Who gets to bitch about who's concept? What's the use of even allowing for this situation to be a possibility?<br /> <br /> Again, this seems like something that should be dealt with by having a conversation with your players; not telling one player they don't have a right to voice opinions regardless of the usefulness of those opinions because of their character concept.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why do you assume there isn't a broad conversation? A game is created as a collaboration between the players and the ST. My rule as an ST is that I'm going to give each player a chance for the spotlight. If someone suggests something off the wall, like a White Howler savior, I take this as a request for a more over the top crazy type game where he might be hanging out with the True King of Garou(at which point I'd delete Albrecht from the setting) really it does depend how the stories mesh who wants what etc. Its a point of give and take. So we work out a the level wonkyness we want to play at and go from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T09:09:25-08:00","id":414065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andresmo23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=407420#post407420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well what i meant was a charecter that was unique but (hopefully) not naturally immpossible, a modern white howler, camerilla tremere outside the paramid, hermetic that sees technocrats as correct but wants to channel science through magick (not a good example but couldent think of anything for mage). That sort of thing</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll try to retype this. I hate this forum sometimes.<br /> A lot of good points all around. I don't mind hooks good characters should have them. But hooks have consequences.<br /> They connect to plot points.<br /> <br /> For example Your hermetic is House Thig which are Order of Hermes' techno magick squad. No problem unless he has some weird politics that put him inline with the Conventions more than the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Your Tremere on the other hand, could have a lot of plot dangling over his head.<br /> Why did he not become part of the pyramid? Was his embraced sanctioned? How did he learn Thaum?<br /> Is he blood bonded to members of Pyramid? Do they still walk the night? If not why not to either question?<br /> <br /> The Tremere will be interested in bringing him into the fold. There are not too many ways of resolving that where he is still a special snowflake.<br /> <br /> <br /> But as other have pointed out what drives this is either a lack of familiarity with the setting or a need to be the center of attention.<br /> And that has to addressed.<br /> <br /> You should not allow something that detracts from the story you and your players want to tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":594,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","user":"Chattnos","date":". 02-21-2015, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T10:34:47-08:00","id":414174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=413909#post413909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you assume there isn't a broad conversation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because your statements so far have directly talked about narrowing the conversation in the face of someone requesting to play something you consider a special snowflake instead of having a broad discussion about it.<br /> <br /> Your stated stance was that a play that wants to play X, they don't get a say in whether or not someone plays something else that can equally impact the tone of the game. That's pretty much saying that there isn't a broad conversation.<br /> <br /> Basically, your posts on this previously seem completely antithetical to:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A game is created as a collaboration between the players and the ST. My rule as an ST is that I'm going to give each player a chance for the spotlight. </div> </div> </div>Because your posts have been about taking someone out of that collaboration and the conversations that help guide the spotlight by virtue of having an inherently high spotlight time character.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If someone suggests something off the wall, like a White Howler savior, I take this as a request for a more over the top crazy type game where he might be hanging out with the True King of Garou(at which point I'd delete Albrecht from the setting)... </div> </div> </div>And this is, again, pretty much not meshing for me with the concept of collaboration. You're assuming a request to play X in a request for a specific mode of play rather than talking about why they want to play X before coming to a conclusion. Inserting this step of assumption before conversation inherently limits the idea of having a broad conversation about what the group wants out of the game; hence my initial assumption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its a point of give and take. So we work out a the level wonkyness we want to play at and go from there. </div> </div> </div>Which we do seem to be in agreement on. This was what I was saying. That it should just be a conversation where the group works things out. Not rules about who gets to &quot;bitch&quot; about which concepts or assumptions about what people want before asking them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T20:28:32-08:00","id":414804,"title":"","content":"Before anything else I have to say I want to point out that I feel that I don't think everyone here is on the same page as to the definition of &quot;snowflakes&quot;. From reading what everyone had to say it seems like some people think that snowflakes are people who only create problem characters that detract from the experience for everyone. While others (myself as an example) see snowflakes as unique character concepts that stand out or break the mold, but do not break the game or experience. They add to it.<br /> <br /> To those who really mean &quot;Problem players who F up the game for everyone&quot; I don't see snowflakes that way. Those &quot;problem players&quot; are &quot;insert derogative word starting with A&quot; and should be dealt with by the gaming group as a whole.<b> People who want to play a White Howler, an Abomination, or a Mummy True Mage, etc... I am not defending these types of players. In my experience these players (not all, but usually) cause problems. </b><br /> <br /> And as to what Heavy Arms said at the bottom of the first page, I totally agree. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=411674#post411674\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...674#post411674</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=407391#post407391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, though - the player characters are already the protagonists, why add an extra-special layer of on top of that? While everyone else is going about their mundane lives - picking up milk, balancing the checkbook - they're going on adventures, or have a nemesis. Even the majority of &quot;splat&quot; NPC's keep it routine - somebody's gotta fill up the car, or drop off the mail.</div> </div> </div> </div>As to allowing players to play their snowflakes, direct quote V20 pg 393<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It could be argued, then, that a player who creates such a character is just trying to be \u201cmore unique\u201d than other vampires. Possibly, but so what? If the goal is to tell a compelling story, to focus on the characters that are, by default, more interesting than any others (that is, your characters), then why not create something that doesn\u2019t exist anywhere else? If you feel compelled to play a Blood Brother that has somehow broken the bonds of the circle and achieved autonomy, then do it (with Storyteller approval). Just be aware that doing so makes a statement about the World of Darkness that playing a Toreador painter does not \u2014 and maybe that\u2019s not a bad thing. </div> </div> </div>I don't play RPG's to be carbon copies of cookie cutter builds or to fade into the background. I play them to be the hero, the villain, the monster, the child, the savior... Comparing my character to the guys who drop off mail and pump the tank seems unfair. Compare me to the Toreador, the Hermetic, the Get of Fenris, the other NPC's who measure up to me. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andresmo23</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=407420#post407420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well what i meant was a charecter that was unique but (hopefully) not naturally immpossible, a modern white howler, camerilla tremere outside the paramid, hermetic that sees technocrats as correct but wants to channel science through magick (not a good example but couldent think of anything for mage). That sort of thing</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember correctly some of the Tremere did escape the Pyramid and are safely living in the Anarch Free States as of the new V20 books. Some &quot;impossible&quot; things are possible already in the WW books.<br /> <br /> All of that said I thought I'd mention the three PC's in the current group I play in. These represent &quot;snowflakes&quot; that I think are acceptable. I leave your personal opinions up to you guys and will take no insult. Feel free to skip what follows, it's not part of the argument. Just an example of what I think is fine in a game.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Aizen - Toreador </b></u><br /> <br /> At the start of the new game I told my ST that I wanted to play a master swordsman and he knew I loved Tories. He suggested I play a Toreador whose &quot;art&quot; was sword fighting. It was a stretch, but opened up some interesting role playing. Resentful Sire who accidentally Embraced me and had to have her Primogen Sire cover everything all up for example. I started off as a veteran of the Setite Blood War in our city with a reputation for combat, but my ST noticed I was roleplaying more of a &quot;Samurai&quot; and not Humanity as it should be. We talked and checked the books. I was role playing the Path of Honorable Accord without even realizing it. So we just swapped it in. It made sense. Later through the game I ended up getting one dot in Vicissitude through plot device/magic item. However the ST was running it like the Parasite from the Umbra. After learning up to Bonecrafting I started weaking, my aura and flesh became even paler, and I was losing 2 blood a day instead of one. I had to seek out a Mage and bargain for him to get the parasite out of me. After it was finally over I was frustrated OOC because I really wanted Horrid Form. <br /> <br /> I never planned on getting Vicissitude, the ST did it to me. But it changed my goals OOC. We talked for a while and I eventually brought up creating my own Discipline and Bloodline that would have one power that was similar to Horrid Form mechanically. But the how? The city has a City Mother spirit that is on the level of an Incarna. And one of her spirits (an information spirit) has access to incredibly powerful items, many cursed, that it sometimes will sell to people. Often times whether it will sell the item at all is more about the person it's selling it to. Very long story short after much debate, searching, researching, and burning my Resources down for the story (had 5 Resources) for $500K I was able to purchase a book from him that has lost secrets and could teach me how to create a new Discipline and Bloodline. But there's still more hitches.<br /> <br /> So the further hurdels? As a running gag, my character has only 1 Int and we have locked it in place there. He allowed me to purchase a merit called &quot;Flashes of Brilliance&quot; (made up) to explain Aizen's sometimes amazing ideas. So now I had to buy up the Research skill and it's my only 5 dot skill. My combat skill is at 4 while everything else is 3 or less. And the book was also written in Latin so I had to buy the language as well. And after all of this and some downtime I will get my new Discipline. And I've already traded Boons for the right to create to childer and have the ghouls ready. <br /> <br /> At the start of the game Aizen was just a Toreador with a miffed sire and a laughable art in the Toreador's eyes. In the end he's become a snowflake and the Progenitor of a Bloodline all because of how he ended up reacting and dealing with Plot as it hit him in the face.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Berny, aka. &quot;Count Morgula&quot; - Child of Osiris</b></u><br /> <br /> At the start of the new game Rob wanted to play something unlike anything he'd ever played before. He also is a bit of a power gamer and wanted as many In Clan Disc as possible. We house ruled that without a teacher all Disc were restricted. You had to pay a Major Boon to learn 1-3 dots for vampire and a Life Boon to learn the 4-5 dots for anything out of clan. So he decided on a Child of Osiris so he'd have the 3 Clan Disc plus Bardo. Then he bought Extra Disc (5) merit and for a gag made his original clan Serpent of Light. The Setites in our city are a major villain group and the ST pulls from the lore in Mummy when setting them up. So Berny was grabbed by the Setites but he thought they were bat shit crazy and the devil incarnate. He went as far in the opposite direction from them as possible. It was an interesting gag that also allowed him to power game to get 5 In Clan to start while we all only had 3. We were OK with it. He also took Phobia: Snakes,heh. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> He started off with 8 Humanity and was role playing it hard being super humane at all times and doing the right thing. It was surprising and out of character for him in real life. But we figured out that he actually really got into the character concept and that his vampire loved humans. He started a late night TV show called &quot;Count Morgula Presents&quot; which is a spoof off of a real life TV that was her in New Orleans called Morgus Presents (kind of like Elvira) to also be closer to them and make their days better by sharing entertainment with them.<br /> <br /> As time went on our characters starting finding unique niches and roles growing into the upper echelon of the power structures in the city. However Berny was not. He wasn't pursuing any major personal goals or even leaning towards an obvious plot line. As I mentioned before the City Mother spirit for the city is on the power level of an Incarna. She's the main Protagonist for the city as the PC's strive to help save the city from the encroaching darkness as Formori, Demons, Sabbat, Specters,etc... try to warp and devour it. The ST took an interesting turn and made her take a personal interest in Berny and has even visited him to just talk to him. His care for the humans in her city, his humane nature, his endeavors to do things to provide jobs and entertainment, and his efforts in stopping the Setites and the Sabbat (we're in a Sabbat War atm) made him stand out. And now he has a personal relationship with an Incarna that has a few of the powerful mages and garou in the city very jealous.<br /> <br /> At the start of the game Berny was just a rules raped character for extra Disciplines and a gag for humor value. In the end he's become a snowflake with one of the most powerful spirit connections any Garou or Mage player would kill for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Trevor - Tremere</b></u><br /> <br /> When the new campaign rolled out Doug was disappointed we were not doing a Zoo game because he plays Mages exclusively. So he picked Tremere of course. He's always run damage control in our games and role played good guys so he thought he'd go dark. He made an ex-Nazi who was there for WW2 as one of the doctors with a Humanity of 6. The one thing that set him apart is that the ST allowed him to take Necromancy. Wraiths are a MASSIVE part of the city and it was more to help out the ST by having someone capable of interacting with them rather than make something up later. But beyond that he was a standard Pyramid climber.<br /> <br /> Time went on and he got obviously frustrated playing a vampire. He also was not enjoying being a darker more evil character. He likes being the good guy. As I mentioned before about the information spirit working for the City Mother, when I was (as Aizen) dealing with him for the book I investigated many of the other options and alternatives he had. It turned out that he supposedly could make someone become a Mage, a Changeling, or a Garou. Obviously all conversation stopped at that point. This was something our ST had never put in the game in over 20 years of running WoD. This spirit called Wyrdly doesn't sell everything he has to everyone. He picks and chooses. And what we found out was that this was something the forces loyal to City Mother had been working on with her direct investment for who knows how many centuries. <br /> <br /> There were three items and they were one shot. Once used they would change you into one of the three. One specific item for just one creature type. The catch wasn't money or the like. Your Avatar would be permanently bonded to City Mother. You would always be in her service, you could never leave the city, and you'd always be reborn/reincarnated there in her service. Doug was willing to take the Flaws and plot hooks to get to be a Mage and also for just the cool points of being a Tremere that got their Avatar back. He agrees, uses the glowing blue crystal shard, and there is a very Highlander Quickening like effect. <br /> <br /> The session ends and Doug says he's going to retire the character since it's a vampire game and the ST tells him no. Play it through. So the next session picks up there and I go and check his pulse. He's still a vampire. He doesn't seem remotely different. The ST opted to use this as the spark, or catalyst, for him becoming mortal again and regaining his Avatar. But he's still going to go through the process of learning and changing, exploring what has been done to him. Almost like a real life year long quest for Golconda that you hear about in other players' games. The ST didn't cheese it but made him an incredibly cool snowflake as he starts to learn what he is becoming. And he didn't make him a vampire mage which would have been stupid.<br /> <br /> At this point he reveals in game that he was never a Nazi. He was a Jew who had infiltrated their ranks in order to hunt Nazi's down. It was obvious that this was him finding a way to not be an evil bastage, but it didn't upset any of us. We let it go through as an under the table retcon and it added additional role playing elements making Trevor more interesting as a person.<br /> <br /> At the start of the game Trevor was vanilla with one ST trick so he could communicate with Wraiths. In the end he's the classic tale of a vampire seeking to regain mortality and their Avatar, but somehow actually succeeding.<br /> <br /> <br /> Every one of our players shines in the spotlight in certain arenas and adds new dynamics to the game. No one detracts from it or overpowers the campaign by derailing anything. It's not the style everyone would like, I know that. But after gaming for over 25 years now the vanilla stuff is a bit boring to me. And the other guys have all been gaming for 30+ years at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4579-skeleton-jack","name":"Skeleton Jack","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T08:02:13-08:00","id":415141,"title":"","content":"Point of Order, what is the difference between a Tremere outside the pyramid and a caitiff with thaum?<br /> From a revised point of view none. <br /> I haven't seen V20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T09:16:36-08:00","id":415259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Point of Order, what is the difference between a Tremere outside the pyramid and a caitiff with thaum? </div> </div> </div>Former are much more hunted by the House and Clan than the latter, which would also be hunted but with less zeal, also the former have a cost break with Auspex, Dominate and Thaumaturgy while Caitiff do not. Last but not least the former were, in Revised, weak against Domination by members of the Pyramid if I remember correctly while the latter bear only Caitiff weakness and in V20 the former are more susceptible to Blood Bonds like all Tremere, two sips is enough for a full bond.<br /> <br /> So there is a difference even in Revised and it continues to be a difference in V20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1629,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","user":"Possessed","date":".  Typo's 02-22-2015, 12:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-22T23:39:16-08:00","id":416220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=414174#post414174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is, again, pretty much not meshing for me with the concept of collaboration. You're assuming a request to play X in a request for a specific mode of play rather than talking about why they want to play X before coming to a conclusion. Inserting this step of assumption before conversation inherently limits the idea of having a broad conversation about what the group wants out of the game; hence my initial assumption.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Sometimes a groups plans just don't work. I am not going to enjoy trying to run a &quot;Normal&quot; game with a White Howler Throwback. I'd rather we quickly get to a &quot;this won't work lets try something else&quot; than trying to hammer in things that just don't work for me. There's nothing wrong with &quot;hey we couldn't come up with an idea for werewolf that we'd all enjoy, lets try something else&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:07:13-08:00","id":416239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=416220#post416220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because assuming what's in someone else's head is antithetical to having a deep discussion for the purposes of collaboration based gaming. You asked me why I assumed you aren't having these broad conversations. I'm answering because you keep saying things that seem to imply you want to skip those discussions. That's in fact what you're saying in this post. That you'd rather quickly move past something because you assume it isn't going to work based on your assumptions of what a given player wants before you've even talked to them about it. It seems like you're arguing for two exclusively different things: having a broad conversation with your group to get everyone on the same page to make sure the more special/snowflake/odd-ball concepts work for the group, and skipping conversations because somethings you assume just don't work without having any discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sometimes a groups plans just don't work. </div> </div> </div>That's the point of having the broad conversation right?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not going to enjoy trying to run a &quot;Normal&quot; game with a White Howler Throwback. </div> </div> </div>What does this even mean? What on earth is a normal game? What does the player want out of playing a WH throwback? You seem to be assuming that the point is to have the story revolve around dodging massive Wyrm attacks to regain Lion as a Totem and take back the Tribe for Gaia... but what if the player wants it as big secret that their character is struggling to balance and live a normal Gaian Garou life while the spirits and fate are conspiring to bring them into the light? Those are two very different games. The second seems a lot easier to run in a &quot;normal&quot; game than the first despite both being WH throwback involving games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd rather we quickly get to a &quot;this won't work lets try something else&quot; than trying to hammer in things that just don't work for me. </div> </div> </div>Of course, but that's part of this whole broad conversation we're both saying should happen. &quot;I can't have fun with X&quot; and fully communicating what X is is important because someone might be saying something you assume is X, but they really mean Y, and hammering that out has value. If the WH thing is a personal peeve for you, maybe it isn't the best example for a theoretical conversation. What's something that's more neutral for you?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's nothing wrong with &quot;hey we couldn't come up with an idea for werewolf that we'd all enjoy, lets try something else&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Again, we are in agreement. My issue is that arriving to this conclusion should come from an actual conversation. Not assumptions and poorly communicated preferences.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T00:39:36-08:00","id":416257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=416239#post416239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What does this even mean? What on earth is a normal game? What does the player want out of playing a WH throwback? You seem to be assuming that the point is to have the story revolve around dodging massive Wyrm attacks to regain Lion as a Totem and take back the Tribe for Gaia... but what if the player wants it as big secret that their character is struggling to balance and live a normal Gaian Garou life while the spirits and fate are conspiring to bring them into the light? Those are two very different games. The second seems a lot easier to run in a &quot;normal&quot; game than the first despite both being WH throwback involving games.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Second isn't one I want to run! So rather than coming to me with the idea and wasting both our times, So if the player wants to play the second thing they know not to come to me to run a game. Seems simple enough to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T10:03:43-08:00","id":416589,"title":"","content":"Which... is the whole point of an actual conversation?<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to sell you on running any particular thing, or trying to say it must be fun for you (and I have no idea if the WH thing is just an example you're using or something you're really so dead set against it's tainting the conversation; and if so what about the WH thing you dislike so much to even try to make better examples)..<br /> <br /> I'm saying that broad conversations don't happen when one person completely shuts down an avenue of discussion without an interest in doing more than just shutting it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T11:05:02-08:00","id":416662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=416589#post416589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which... is the whole point of an actual conversation?<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to sell you on running any particular thing, or trying to say it must be fun for you (and I have no idea if the WH thing is just an example you're using or something you're really so dead set against it's tainting the conversation; and if so what about the WH thing you dislike so much to even try to make better examples)..<br /> <br /> I'm saying that broad conversations don't happen when one person completely shuts down an avenue of discussion without an interest in doing more than just shutting it down.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The particular example you suggest hits alot of my &quot;I don't want to run this&quot; issues(trying to &quot;normalize&quot; snowflakeness, Rejection of Destiny, Potential problems with Ic/ooc knowledge with other players). I have personal rules that I generally won't budge on, I have players who have preferences on theirown. For example one won't play Nmage, the other won't play Omage I don't ask them both when I have a vague desire to run mage. I am sure if we were regular gaming buddies I'd come to know your preferences as readily and thus there would be things you wouldn't like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T14:36:08-08:00","id":416894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=416662#post416662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The particular example you suggest hits alot of my &quot;I don't want to run this&quot; issues</div> </div> </div> </div>I was gathering that, which is why I've tried to point that out as potential distraction from the conversation. I can come up with different examples if needed that don't touch on these things. But I don't think it's that much to ask you to step back a bit from your personal preferences for a conversation about generalities. Reading everything I wrote under the lens of, &quot;OMG I hate X&quot; when X is just one example doesn't really help me know if you're getting what I'm trying to say instead of just reacting to stuff you don't like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (trying to &quot;normalize&quot; snowflakeness, Rejection of Destiny, Potential problems with Ic/ooc knowledge with other players). </div> </div> </div>I think it's worth noting that when talking about a &quot;normal&quot; WtA game... the idea I posed is basically Jonas Albrecht's story as a Howler instead of a Silver Fang. And Albrecht is presented as a core example of long term player character. So a lot of people are going to come into the game assuming this is a normal thing that might come up.<br /> <br /> I also find the idea of &quot;normalizing snowflakeness&quot; as a bad thing baffling. Isn't the idea of collaborating and compromising a concept seen as a snowflake to be less extreme so that it doesn't ruin the fun of everyone else and attempt to normalize it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have personal rules that I generally won't budge on, I have players who have preferences on theirown. For example one won't play Nmage, the other won't play Omage I don't ask them both when I have a vague desire to run mage. I am sure if we were regular gaming buddies I'd come to know your preferences as readily and thus there would be things you wouldn't like. </div> </div> </div>Yes. We all have personal preferences that we have no interest in changing.<br /> <br /> But that's the thing. You know those things because you've talked to your players about them. They know yours because you've talked to them.<br /> <br /> The key thing is having talked to your group. Not skipping it. Obviously you don't need to have it again if everyone there has already had it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T19:22:35-08:00","id":417079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/407159-special-snowflakes?p=416894#post416894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I think it's worth noting that when talking about a &quot;normal&quot; WtA game... the idea I posed is basically Jonas Albrecht's story as a Howler instead of a Silver Fang. And Albrecht is presented as a core example of long term player character. So a lot of people are going to come into the game assuming this is a normal thing that might come up.<br /> <br /> I also find the idea of &quot;normalizing snowflakeness&quot; as a bad thing baffling. Isn't the idea of collaborating and compromising a concept seen as a snowflake to be less extreme so that it doesn't ruin the fun of everyone else and attempt to normalize it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It bothers me as a person? It just eats at me on some level? Its not a rational reaction it. Albrecht is a fun character to read about but is not the sort of character I'd want to run with, not because I think the story is bad but because I just don't find running those sorts of things fun. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes. We all have personal preferences that we have no interest in changing.<br /> <br /> But that's the thing. You know those things because you've talked to your players about them. They know yours because you've talked to them.<br /> <br /> The key thing is having talked to your group. Not skipping it. Obviously you don't need to have it again if everyone there has already had it. </div> </div> </div>Yes, I am working from this is a long term group. But if it were a new player/group forming I'd probably go over this sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}